{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/704697-ideas-for-locations-in-1940s-50s-setting","id":704697,"title":"Ideas for locations in 1940s/50s Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-17T05:21:02-07:00","id":704697,"title":"Ideas for locations in 1940s/50s Setting","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I'm new here, but currently planning a DtD game with 2 players and myself as ST (I have ST experience in CtL with a 4 player group). The setting is supposed to be 1949 in a fictional U.S. metropolitan area called Columbia City on the East Coast. Now I am having some trouble finding good ideas for locations, especially combining the scifi aspect of Demon with the low-tech era that was the 40s/50s.<br /> <br /> The players haven't yet created their characters although one of them told me he is interested in playing a private detective-type demon. So ideas can be broad, no final decisions being made on my part as of now.<br /> <br /> Some ideas that I have had for locations (very clich\u00e9, at least to me):<br /> - Old Industrial District, with high crime rate, dark alleyways and muddy apartment buildings.<br /> - Underground tunnels, maybe a sewer system. I really like sewer scenarios and haven't had the chance of building one into my CtL game.<br /> - Luxurious hotel/club, high society, red carpet.<br /> <br /> My problem seems to be that I can't think of anything mundane that allows for some form of high-tech in a 40s/50s scenario. Maybe a radio station?<br /> <br /> I'd really love some help on the topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> A little inspiration is always nice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T14:13:06-07:00","id":705722,"title":"","content":"Russian Consulate<br /> A University (large number of folks will be coming through on the GI Bill)<br /> Levittsvilles<br /> Shipping ports<br /> Rail stations/bus transportation/ railcar lines(possibly being dismantled by auto industry)<br /> TV and/or radio station (possible Infrastructure)<br /> DOD Contractors<br /> A prison (during this time period the federal government is using prisoners, among others, to test the effects of LSD, G-M activity)<br /> An airport (commercial air travel is becoming available at this time)<br /> <br /> Edit: Not sure how I missed this one but, <u>fallout shelters</u>. The G-M is an open justification for time travel, parallel/alternate timelines as a source of unease and horror. By 1955, the US has a massive number of nuclear armed bombers on standby, and even before then, the threat of nuclear war was a thing that drove public fears and government policy. You're to throw nuclear scenarios at the players, &quot;official&quot; history be damned. The cold war can go hot, and the G-M can sever the timeline and put it in the apocalypse vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 11-06-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T20:15:04-07:00","id":706185,"title":"","content":"During WWII the U.S. government built a train rail traversing part of the east coast for the war effort. The tracks were used for the often secret transport of personnel and supplies and in places like New York included secret underground rail stations. If your city is on the east coast it too could include secret underground rails and stations. This would also be a great place for hidden tech and the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T12:20:23-07:00","id":707229,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys! I like the secret underground rails idea. Sounds like a good setting for infrastructure, yes, and maybe also a good place to hide God Machine cults.<br /> <br /> I didn't know about the drug-testing part with the prisons. And didn't think about airports, actually quite a good way of having some more technology included. Russian Consulate is something that seems very Cold War to me. Now, obviously Cold War starts around that time, so it would be possible but I feel like it has more of an early 60s vibe to it. Still a great suggestion as time moves on within the chronicle. I might give it a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}